  "id": "step-up",
  "name": "Forward Step-Up",
  "definition": "A lead-limb closed-chain compound step in which the lead foot begins on a raised platform and raises the body without propulsive help from the trail leg. The roster owns two source-exact forward fixtures: a complete 21-centimeter bodyweight sequence with bilateral top support and both feet returning to the floor, and an approximately 38-centimeter two-dumbbell sequence that repeats one lead side while leaving terminal trail-foot contact and descent order unreported. The contract preserves those unknowns rather than converting them into a generic continuous step-up. Other box heights, trail-leg propulsion, hand support, stair climbing, step-downs, and lateral, crossover, diagonal, reverse, explosive, or machine-stepping tasks remain outside this family.",
